From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:20:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: serialize postMessage sender security origin

MessageEvent.origin is the sender's security origin, not the origin of its
Location URL. about:blank and srcdoc inherit a tuple origin while their URL
origin remains null. Using Location.getOrigin therefore delivered null from
these same-origin senders even though window.origin was already correct.

Read Window.getOrigin (Frame.origin with opaque fallback null) and retain the
existing synchronous copy into the queued callback arena. Keep incumbent-source
selection, cloning, source identity, dispatch trust, and targetOrigin behavior
unchanged. Mark the now-unused implicit Frame parameter anonymous.

An isolated local Chrome/native reduction covers HTTP, blank, document.write,
srcdoc, opaque data and blob senders. All six message-origin/source/trust cases
match after this change; the separate document.write URL-update mismatch remains.
All 1658 existing upstream tests pass; no new tests are added.

This was found during Sephora handoff diagnosis but the observed live SDK
messages did not exhibit the inherited-origin mismatch. It is a separate API
fix, not an established binary-submission blocker or a verification workaround.
---
 src/browser/webapi/Window.zig | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/browser/webapi/Window.zig b/src/browser/webapi/Window.zig
index 11e3dd8..5d7a1d5 100644
--- a/src/browser/webapi/Window.zig
+++ b/src/browser/webapi/Window.zig
@@ -889,7 +889,7 @@ pub fn stop(self: *Window) void {
     self._frame.stopLoading();
 }
 
-pub fn postMessage(self: *Window, message: js.Value, target_origin: ?[]const u8, transfer: ?[]const *MessagePort, frame: *Frame) !void {
+pub fn postMessage(self: *Window, message: js.Value, target_origin: ?[]const u8, transfer: ?[]const *MessagePort, _: *Frame) !void {
     // For now, we ignore targetOrigin checking and just dispatch the message
     // In a full implementation, we would validate the origin
     _ = target_origin;
@@ -924,7 +924,7 @@ pub fn postMessage(self: *Window, message: js.Value, target_origin: ?[]const u8,
     errdefer cloned.release();
 
     // Origin should be the source window's origin (where the message came from)
-    const origin = try source_window._location.getOrigin(&frame.js.execution);
+    const origin = source_window.getOrigin();
     const callback = try arena.create(PostMessageCallback);
     callback.* = .{
         .arena = arena,
